sieve-filter-v1
; A fractal's ruleset (sieve-fractal-v1, SPECIFICATIONS 12.0t, core/include/sieve/fractal.hpp) written as a
; filter, so the text line over ascii96 with it ticked is the fractal dimension: "sieve-fractal-v1", then
; "substitution" (symbols 0-9 and a-z) or "lsystem ANGLE" (1 to 359 degrees; letters and + - [ ] |),
; "axiom WORD" and one or more "rule SYMBOL WORD" (an L-system's only for letters), every word 1 to 64
; symbols and every line ending in a line feed. One thing the reader asks and a walk does not: that the
; rules stand in the order of their symbols, each once. So its survivors are the reader's rulesets with
; their rules in any order; tools/check_formats.py checks every other verdict.
; Written by tools/grammars.py (the grammar is there; this table is what it compiles to).

id        format-fractal
version   1
author    Edward James Gordon (written with Claude)
origin    ai-directed
lines     text
symbols   ascii96
describe  One sieve-fractal-v1 ruleset (its rules' order aside): the fractal dimension's line, each ruleset at its address (IDEAS 19.191, 19.235).

class     c0    @0                       ; \n
class     c1    @1                       ;  
class     c2    @12 @60 @62 @93          ; +[]|
class     c3    @14                      ; -
class     c4    @17                      ; 0
class     c5    @18                      ; 1
class     c6    @19                      ; 2
class     c7    @20                      ; 3
class     c8    @21..@22                 ; 45
class     c9    @23..@26                 ; 6789
class     c10   @34..@59                 ; ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ
class     c11   @66                      ; a
class     c12   @67                      ; b
class     c13   @68                      ; c
class     c14   @69 @72..@73 @75..@76 @81..@82 @88 @91 ; dghjkpqwz
class     c15   @70                      ; e
class     c16   @71                      ; f
class     c17   @74                      ; i
class     c18   @77                      ; l
class     c19   @78                      ; m
class     c20   @79                      ; n
class     c21   @80                      ; o
class     c22   @83                      ; r
class     c23   @84                      ; s
class     c24   @85                      ; t
class     c25   @86                      ; u
class     c26   @87                      ; v
class     c27   @89                      ; x
class     c28   @90                      ; y

